schema: "0.3"
id: echo-of-manifestation-env-time-dilation-pocket
type: image
service: gemini

prompt:
  text: >
    Dark fantasy concept art of a Time Dilation Pocket — a safe zone within the Twilight
    Zone where the player can rest and transmute safely without spawning chimeras. The
    composition centers on a crystalline bubble of calm, roughly 10 meters across, its
    surface a translucent membrane that refracts the hostile Twilight Zone outside into
    distorted but clearly separate shapes. Inside the bubble, warm amber light suffuses
    everything — not from any single source but from the air itself, as if time and safety
    have a warm color. The ground inside is stable: flat stone with no dissolving edges,
    perhaps a small alcove with a simple bench and a smaller version of the alchemy shrine.
    Essence nodes rest on the ground, glowing amber, harvestable. Outside the bubble, the
    Twilight Zone presses in — indigo darkness, moving shadows, hostile geometry visible
    through the membrane but unable to penetrate. The contrast is the entire point: warm
    safety inside, cold hostility outside, separated by a membrane that feels fragile.
    Time effects are visible inside — dust motes move slowly, ripples in water take longer
    to settle, as if time itself is thicker here. A few moments of peace before the player
    must venture back out. Painterly style, the amber interior light bleeding outward
    through the crystalline membrane, meeting the indigo dark at the boundary.
  negative: "bright, cheerful, cartoon, anime, clean magic, modern interior, cozy cottage, colorful palette, bright light, clean sci-fi force field, generic safe room, low detail, flat shading"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024
    aspect_ratio: "3:2"

tags: [environment, gameplay, safe-zone, time-dilation, rest-area, concept-art, dark-fantasy]
